backend_architecture.pagination_convention:
ALL list endpoints support optional pagination via query params: page, limit.
If 'page' is NOT provided → returns flat array (backward compatible for dropdowns/Kanban).
If 'page' IS provided → returns:
  {
    data: [...],
    pagination: {
      total: number,
      page: number,
      limit: number,
      totalPages: number
    }
  }
Default limit: 10. Minimum page: 1. Minimum limit: 1.

backend_architecture.validation_rules:
Project Name: - 3 to 100 characters - Regex: /^[a-zA-Z0-9\s]+$/ (alphanumeric + spaces only, no special characters) - Must NOT start with a digit: /^\d/.test(name) returns false - Must be unique within the organization (case-insensitive) - Response on failure: 400 with JSON { error: "message" }
Task Title: - Must not be empty - Regex: /^[a-zA-Z0-9\s]+$/ (alphanumeric + spaces only) - Must NOT start with a digit - Must be unique within the same project (case-insensitive) - Response on failure: 400 with JSON { error: "message" }
User Name (invite/create): - Alphanumeric + spaces only (special characters not allowed)
Passwords: - Minimum length enforced (check controller for exact value) - Hashed with bcryptjs (saltRounds: 10)

backend_architecture.how_to_add_endpoint:
1. Add controller function to appropriate file in src/controllers/.
   Pattern (with express-async-errors — NO try/catch needed):
     export const myEndpoint = async (req, res) => {
       const { param } = req.params;
       const { field } = req.body;
       const { queryParam } = req.query;
       const { id, role, organizationId } = req.user;  // from authenticate middleware
       const result = await prisma.model.findMany({ where: { organizationId } });
       res.json(result);
     };

2. Export function from controller file.

3. Add route to appropriate router in src/routes/:
     import { myEndpoint } from '../controllers/myController.js';
     router.get('/path', authenticate, authorize('ADMIN'), myEndpoint);
     Note: router.use(authenticate) is already at top of most route files.

4. If new route file needed, register in src/server.js:
     import myRoutes from './routes/myRoutes.js';
     app.use('/api/myresource', myRoutes);

5. For Prisma queries:
     import { PrismaClient } from '@prisma/client';
     const prisma = new PrismaClient();
     (Each controller file creates its own PrismaClient instance.)

6. Error responses:
     return res.status(400).json({ error: 'Validation message' });
     return res.status(404).json({ error: 'Not found' });
     return res.status(403).json({ error: 'Forbidden' });
     // Throwing errors also works (caught by errorHandler middleware)

7. For Prisma schema changes:
     Edit backend/prisma/schema.prisma
     Run: npx prisma migrate dev --name describe_your_change
     Run: npx prisma generate
